-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  test_asserts_outside.pcpp - Unit testing compliance: an assert outside a test

  An assert in a routine or the body (not in a test block) that does not
  hold prints <file>:<line>: <message> to stderr, after what the program had
  printed, and ends the program with exit code 1 on every target; one that
  holds does nothing. Nothing after it runs, so no heap report either.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\test_asserts_outside.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\test_asserts_outside.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    before
    held
    <DIR>/test_asserts_outside.pcpp:42: testAssertEqualInt failed: expected 1, got 2
  EXITCODE: 1
  <DIR> is the folder this file is in, as the compiler prints it
  (its full path, forward slashes).
  stdout and stderr in the order written; the debug heap report does not run.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe test_asserts_outside;

begin
  println("before");
  testAssertTrue(true);
  println("held");
  testAssertEqualInt(1, 2);
  println("never printed");
end.
